diction setup; 1 mark for concluding statement.", "difficulty": "Medium"}, {"id": "q-b-2", "text": "Find the roots of the quadratic equation sqrt(3)x^2 + 10x + 7*sqrt(3) = 0 by factorisation.", "bloom": "Apply", "marks": 2, "rubric": "1 mark for splitting middle term 3x + 7x; 1 mark for correct roots x = -sqrt(3), -7/sqrt(3).", "difficulty": "Medium"}], "section_id": "sec-b", "marks_per_q": 2, "instructions": "Questions 21 to 25 carry 2 marks each with very short answers."}, {"name": "Section C", "type": "short_answer_2", "questions": [{"id": "q-c-1", "text": "Prove that: (sin theta - 2 sin^3 theta) / (2 cos^3 theta - cos theta) = tan theta.", "bloom": "Analyze", "marks": 3, "rubric": "1 mark for taking common terms; 1 mark for identity substitution; 1 mark for simplifying to tan theta.", "difficulty": "Medium"}], "section_id": "sec-c", "marks_per_q": 3, "instructions": "Questions 26 to 31 carry 3 marks each with short answers."}, {"name": "Section D", "type": "long_answer", "questions": [{"id": "q-d-1", "text": "A motor boat whose speed is 18 km/h in still water takes 1 hour more to go 24 km upstream than to return downstream to the same spot. Find the speed of the stream.", "bloom": "Evaluate", "marks": 5, "rubric": "2 marks for formulating equation 24/(18-s) - 24/(18+s) = 1; 2 marks for solving quadratic s^2 + 48s - 324 = 0; 1 mark for s = 6 km/h.", "difficulty": "Hard"}], "section_id": "sec-d", "marks_per_q": 5, "instructions": "Questions 32 to 35 carry 5 marks each with detailed step-by-step working."}, {"name": "Section E", "type": "case_study", "questions": [{"id": "q-e-1", "text": "Case Study: India Gate Shadow Measurement. A student standing 30 m away observes top of monument at 60 deg elevation. Sub-part (i) Find height of monument (2M). Sub-part (ii) Find distance if angle becomes 45 deg (2M).", "bloom": "Create", "marks": 4, "rubric": "2 marks for sub-part (i) h = 30*sqrt(3) m; 2 marks for sub-part (ii) distance = 30*sqrt(3) m.", "difficulty": "Hard"}], "section_id": "sec-e", "marks_per_q": 4, "instructions": "Case study based questions are compulsory. Questions 36 to 38 carry 4 marks each with sub-parts."}]', '2026-09-23', NULL, 'ready', '2026-09-16 19:14:55.333909+05:30', '2026-09-16 19:14:55.333909+05:30');
